# id Software's source (and the q2tools compiler) that the C oracles build and the explorer's labs
# quote, fetched by scripts/fetch-id-source.sh into quake2ts/.id-source/<dir>.
#
# Each line: <dir> <git tree> <repo> <commit> <path in that repo>
# The tree is what is checked: git names a tree by the hash of every file in it, so a match means
# the files are byte for byte the ones pinned, wherever they came from. The commit is where to get
# it upstream; if upstream is gone, the same trees are fetched from this repo's commit 3dada0f
# (the last on main that carried them at the repository root, where <dir> was the path). That copy
# of q2tools left out upstream's .github and .gitignore, so its tree differs and only upstream serves it.
